$DATUM 68-12-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Nucleophilic Aromatic Substitution (16-37). The target
aryldithiocarbamates 16-37 were obtained by a nucleophilic aromatic
substitution using the following protocol. To a solution of
dithiocarbamic acid triethylammonium salt (see Supporting Information, p
S2) (1.2 mmol) in N,N-dimethylformamide (5 mL) was added
2,4-dinitrofluorobenzene (1 mmol). The mixture was stirred overnight at
room temperature, dissolved in water, and extracted with dichloromethane.
The organic phase was dried over sodium sulfate and evaporated under
reduced pressure. Crystallization from ethanol afforded the pure product.
In some cases further purification using column chromatography (silica
gel, ethyl acetate/hexane, 3:7 v/v) was needed. 2,4-Dinitrophenyl
4-Benzhydrylpiperazine-1-carbodithioate (16). Yield 80-95%. Mp 157-159
°C. 1H NMR (CDCl3): 8.75 (d, 1H, J = 2.32 Hz), 8.32 (dd, 1H, J = 6.16
Hz), 7.78 (d, 1H, J = 8.64 Hz), 7.36-7.11 (m, 10H), 4.23 (s, 1H), 4.01
(t, 2H, J = 4.84 Hz), 3.99 (t, 2H, J = 4.84 Hz), 2.48 (t, 4H, J = 4.84
Hz). 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ (ppm) 189.90, 151.20, 147.90, 141.67, 139.35,
135.14, 128.81, 127.82, 127.47, 126.19, 120.44, 75.56, 52.16, 51.94,
51.64, 51.23 . HRMS: [M + H]+ = 495.113 34.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Sanger reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Pharmacological Evaluation of
2,4-Dinitroaryldithiocarbamate Derivatives as Novel Monoacylglycerol
Lipase Inhibitors
