$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure B: To a 10 mL glass tube,
CuBr (2.8 mg, 0.02 mmol), 1,10-phenanthroline (3.6 mg, 0.02 mmol), AgSCF3
(62.7 mg, 0.3 mmol), and arylhalide (0.2 mmol) were dissolved in dry DMF
(1 mL) under N2 atmosphere. The tube was sealed and the mixture was
stirred at the corresponding temperature for 6 h. After completion of the
reaction, the mixture was directly subjected to flash column
chromatography on silica gel with a gradient eluent of petroleum ether
and ethyl acetate (range from 20:1 to 5:1). The product.
N-phenyl-2-((trifluoromethyl)thio)benzamide (6b) This reaction was
conducted with procedure B in 0.2 mmol scale. The residue was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel with a gradient eluent of petroleum
ether and ethyl acetate (6:1 - 3:1). The product 6b (56 mg, 95% yield) as
white solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.89 (br, 1H), 7.76 (t, J = 8.4 Hz
1H), 7.64 (t, J = 4.8 Hz, 1H), 7.59 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H), 7.50 (m, 2H),
7.36 (t, J = 8.0 Hz , 2H), 7.17 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 165.6, 141.7, 137.4, 136.8, 131.0, 130.7, 129.4 (q, J = 307 Hz),
129.1, 128.5, 125.0, 122.7, 120.2. 19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3) δ -41.64 (s).
HRMS: m/z (ESI) calculated [M+H]+: 298.0508 , measured: 298.0510.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copper-Catalyzed Trifluoromethylthiolation of Aryl Halides with Diverse
Directing Groups
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
