$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1,4-Bis(phenylthio)benzene (3a); Typical
Procedure. A flame-dried test tube with a magnetic stirring bar was
charged with CuBr (7 mg, 0.05 mmol), ligand (15 mg, 0.1 mmol), Cs2CO3
(489 mg, 1.5 mmol), thiophenol (121 mg, 1.1 mmol), p-dibromobenzene (118
mg, 0.5 mmol), and DMF (1.5 mL) under argon. The mixture was stirred at
130 °C for 48 h, then cooled to r.t. and the resulting mixture was
extracted with EtOAc (3 x 25 mL). The combined organic layers were dried
(Na2SO4) and concentrated under vacuum. The residue was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel with PE as eluent.
1,4-Bis(phenylthio)benzene (3a) as white solid (CAS: 3459-94-7), yield
95%. mp 81.6-82.1 °C (Lit. mp 81.3 °C). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.35
(d, J = 7.2 Hz, 4 H), 7.32-7.28 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 4 H), 7.27-7.23 (t, J =
7.2 Hz, 2 H), 7.21 (s, 4 H).13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 135.2, 135.1,
131.6, 131.3, 129.5, 127.6. GC-MS (EI): m/z = 294 [M]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown
