$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A. Representative Synthesis of 3a A mixture of
hexafluorobenzene (280 mg, 1.5 mmol) and
N-(tert-Butoxycarbonyl)-L-cysteine methyl ester (706 mg, 3 mmol) and
Na3PO4 (600 mg, 3.7 mmol) was magnetically stirred in 15 mL of dry
acetonitrile for 4.5 h at room temperature under an atmosphere of dry
argon. The resulting mixture was filtered through a pad of celite on a
glass-fritted filter, evaporated in vacuo and subsequently purified on a
silica gel column (product elutes with 4:1 hexanes/EtOAc solvent
mixture). Obtained fractions containing product were combined and dried
in vacuo to afford the title compound 3a.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Perfluoroaryl-Cysteine SNAr Chemistry Approach to Unprotected Peptide
Stapling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
