$DATUM 4-[(2-Methoxy-2-oxoethyl)thio]-3-nitrobenzoic Acid 2. A solution of
3-nitro-4-fluorobenzoic acid 1 (185 g, 1 mol), methyl mercaptoacetate
(116.6 g, 1.1 mol), and sodium acetate (90.2 g, 1.1 mol) in water (500
mL) was stirred at 80-90 °C for 6 h. The reaction mixture was slowly
cooled to 10 °C at stirring. The formed precipitate was filtered off,
washed with water (5 x 100 mL), and dried in vacuo to afford 257.5 g
(95%) of acid 2, which was used at the next step without further
purification. (LC/MS m/z 271.251 00 (M + 1)).
