$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Representative Procedure for the Synthesis of 4-Methoxyphenyl Phenyl
Sulfide (Table 2, entry 2). An oven-dried 4 mL vial containing a stirrer
bar was charged with an 4-methoxyphenyl bromide (93.5 mg, 0.5 mmol),
catalyst (6.5 mg, 2 mol%) and KOtBu (84.2 mg, 0.75 mmol) in the glove box
and sealed with a cap containing a PTFE / Silicone septum. Toluene (1 mL)
and thiophenyl (0.60 mmol) were injected sequentially. The mixture was
stirred at 100°C for 6 h. The crude was purified by column chromatography
on silica gel with petroleum ether as eluent. 101.7 mg (0.47 mmol, 94 %)
of the product as colorless liquid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.41 (d, J
= 8.8 Hz, 2H), 7.25-7.21 (m, 2H), 7.17-7.11 (m, 3H), 6.89 (d, J = 8.8 Hz,
2H), 3.81 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 159.8, 138. 6, 135.3,
128.9, 128.3, 125.8, 124.4, 115.0, 55.3. EIMS m/z: 216 (M+)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM catalyst prepared and used, alternative preparation shown, the article
was retracted by the corresponding author in "Synlett", 2014, 25(5),750
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Carbon-sulfur coupling reactions catalyzed by Pd-NHC complex
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Shi, Yanhui; Cai, Zhengyuan; Guan, Pei; Pang, Guangsheng
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2011), (14), 2090-2096

