$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the Coupling reaction A
mixture of iodotoluene (262 mg, 1.2 mmol), thiophenol (103 μL, 1.0 mmol),
and Cs2CO3 (652 mg, 2.0 mmol) was dissolved in DMF. Subsequently, Fe2O3
(16 mg, 0.1 mmol), Cu(OAc)2 (18 mg, 0.1 mmol), TMEDA (30 μL, 0.2 mmol)
were added to this mixture. The vial was sealed and the mixture was then
irradiated for 10 min at 135 °C. The reaction was then cooled to ambient
temperature, and the crude reaction mixture was diluted with
dichloromethane and filtered. The filtrate was washed twice with brine,
and the combined aqueous phases were extracted twice with
dichloromethane.The organic layers were dried using Na2SO4, concentrated
and purified by flash column chromatography (petroleum ether) to yield
the expected product 1a (188 mg, 94% yield). The identity and purity of
the product was confirmed by 1H and 13 NMR spectroscopic analysis.
Diphenyl sulfide (1a) Following the general procedure using iodobenzene
and thiophenol provided diphenyl sulfide. Phenyl m-tolyl sulfide (1c)
Following the general procedure using 3-iodotoluene and thiophenol
provided phenyl m-tolyl sulfide. Yield 94%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ
7.34-7.18 (m, 9H), 2.33 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 139.0,
136.1, 135.2, 131.8, 130.7, 129.1, 129.0, 128.3, 128.0, 127.5, 127.1,
126.8, 21.3. MS (EI, m/z): 200 [M]+; HRMS (EI): Calcd. for C13H12S [M]+:
200.0660; Found:200.0661.
