allylation and allenylation reactions (Table 4) Reaction with
4-iodobenzaldehyde (4c) (Table 4, entry 4, 5d) : Yellow oil. 1H-NMR(400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.38 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 2H), 7.31 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 2H), 4.93
(s, 1H), 4.86 (s, 1H), 4.79 (td, J = 6.7, 2.2 Hz, 1H), 3.36 (septet, J =
6.6 Hz, 1H), 2.41 (d, J = 6.7 Hz, 2H), 2.14 (br, 1H), 1.80 (s, 3H),
1.28(d, J = 6.6 Hz, 6H); 13C-NMR(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 142.7, 142.2, 134.4,
132.1, 126.2, 114.3, 71.0, 48.4, 38.3, 23.1, 22.3; IR (Neat) 3399, 3074,
2965, 2927, 2865, 2727, 1909, 1794, 1648, 1599, 1491, 1241, 892 cm-1;
HRMS (EI) calcd for C14H20OS M+ 236.1235, found 236.1236.
