$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of Diacids (1,
2). To a suspension of NaH (0.23 g, 9.58 mmol) in DMF (10-15 mL),
2-mercaptobenzoic acid (0.500 g, 3.25 mmol) was added and the reaction
mixture was stirred at room temperature until the evolution of hydrogen
gas stopped. 2-Chlorobenzoic acid or 2-chloro-4-nitrobenzoic acid (3.25
mmol) and Cu2O (0.0715 g, 0.50 mmol) were then added and the resulting
mixture was refluxed under a nitrogen atmosphere for 5 h with continuous
stirring. The residue was cooled, poured onto ice, and filtered. The
solid obtained was extracted with diethyl ether (30 mL) and the filtrate
and washings were combined and then concentrated to give a solid that was
recrystallized from ethyl acetate and petroleum ether (1:5, 60-80 °C).
2,2'-Thiodibenzoic acid (1): Yield 94%, pale yellow solid. m.p. 223 °C
(lit.: 227-230 °C). IR: 2510-3527, 1689, 746. 1H NMR: 7.25 (d, 2H, J= 7
Hz, ArH), 7.56 (t, 2H, J= 8 Hz, ArH), 7.96 (d, 2H, J= 7 Hz, ArH), 8.18
(d, 2H, J= 8 Hz, ArH). 13C NMR: 125.4, 126.6, 128.5, 132.1, 133.7, 140.2,
168.4. Anal. Calcd. for C14H10O4S: C, 61.3; H, 3.67; S, 11.7. Found: C,
61.0; H, 3.68; S, 12.1. log P: 3.251.
