$DATUM Methyl 4-(benzylthio)-3-nitrobenzoate (1) Methyl 4-chloro-3-nitrobenzoate
(2 g, 9.30 mmol) was dissolved in methanol (9.3 mL) then,
diisopropylethylamine (DIPEA; 1.95 mL, 11.17 mmol) and benzyl mercaptan
(1.14 mL, 9.68 mmol) were added at 0°C. The reaction mixture was stirred
at room temperature for 9 h. The yellow suspension was washed with cold
methanol and hexane. The resulting was dried in vacuo to yield as a
yellow powder. (94%, 2.66 g, 8.77 mmol). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.83
(d, J = 1.9 Hz, 1H), 8.11 (dd, J = 8.5, 1.9 Hz, 1H), 7.50 (d, J = 8.6 Hz,
1H), 7.43-7.38 (m, 2H), 7.37-7.26 (m, 3H), 4.23 (s, 2H), 3.93 (s, 3H)
ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 164.88, 145.06, 143.82, 134.18, 133.58,
129.03, 128.97, 128.93, 127.99, 127.24, 126.68, 126.49, 52.60, 37.54 ppm;
High Resolution MS (ESI): Calculated for C15H13NO4S[M+Na]+: 326.0463,
Found:326.0443.
