$DATUM 5-(4-Acetamidophenylthio)-2-nitroaniline (1b). 5-Chloro-2-nitroaniline
(15.7 g, 90.8 mmol) and potassium tert-butoxide (10.2 g, 90.8mmol) was
added to a solution of 4-acetamidothiophenol (14.5 g, 86.5 mmol) in
2-propanol (600 mL). The mixture was refluxed for 4 h. After cooling,
water was added and the resultant solid was collected by filtration.
Desiccation in vacuo gave 1b as a yellow solid (24.65 g, 94%): 1H NMR
(DMSO-d6 ) δ 10.24 (s, 1H), 7.87 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 7.74 (d, J = 8.4
Hz, 2H), 7.50 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.45 (s, 2H), 6.54 (d, J = 2.0 Hz,
1H), 6.29 (dd, J = 8.8 and 2.0 Hz, 1H), 2.09 (s, 3H); MS m/z 304 (M + 1).
